# The differences between the exported surface of every published module and the surface of its last
# tag, one line per object.
#
#   module ~ class ~ object ~ change ~ disposition ~ reason
#
# Read by .dev/validate/apidiff.sh. This is not a suppression list: every line is a claim the run has to
# satisfy. A difference with no line here fails the check, and a line whose difference no longer occurs
# fails it just as loudly — the change it files is gone, or a release moved the tag past it, so the line
# has to go. A line whose class or change text no longer matches what the run measures fails too: the row
# then describes a different fact than the one that occurs, and has to be rewritten. That is what keeps
# the file the measured list rather than a remembered one.
#
# The class and the change are apidiff's own words, measured, never asserted:
#
#   incompatible  a signature changed, a symbol or package was removed, a constant's value changed, a
#                 type lost comparability, an interface a third party may implement grew a method, or a
#                 named type changed identity (apidiff prints `changed from T to T` when the text is the
#                 same and the type behind it is not, such as a type that became an alias of a type in
#                 another package). Each of these is a decision a release has to make before its tag.
#
#   compatible    an addition. Allowed on a minor release, not on a patch one — which is what makes a row
#                 of this class on a frozen major a finding rather than routine.
#
# The disposition is the decision the row carries:
#
#   keep          ships on this major — backwards compatible, a security repair, or a defect repair whose
#                 remedy cannot be compatible. Has to say why.
#   cut           leaves this major before its next tag, and lives on the next major. Has to say why.
#   unclassified  measured, not yet decided. The reason may be empty, because "measured, undecided" is the
#                 whole claim, and a generic reason would be a reason nobody can review. The gate counts
#                 these rows: that number is the work left before a tag.
#
# The tag each module is compared with is deliberately not a field. The run reads it from git and prints
# it beside the module, so this file cannot carry a version that has gone stale. Every field is compared
# for exact equality, so nothing here is a pattern: a `*` in an object is a pointer receiver in apidiff's
# own spelling, never a wildcard. A `~` inside a field is refused, being the separator. Fields are
# trimmed, so the columns may be aligned.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Seeded on 2026-09-04 from the branch fix/v3-stabilization-sweep at a8ae204: 312 rows on v3 against
# v3.13.0 (101 incompatible, 211 compatible), 90 rows on the v3 integrations against their last tags,
# and none on v1, v2 or their integrations, whose unreleased changes are patch-level by measurement.
# Every row landed unclassified except the two on the message bus transport's Close, adjudicated before
# this band existed. The rows are the work list of the step that cuts from v3 what is not backwards
# compatible before v3.14.0; a decided row replaces `unclassified` with `keep` or `cut` and a reason.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

integrations/bunorm/migrate/v3 ~ compatible ~ SetDefaultRunnerOption ~ added ~ keep ~ the process-default door bun's fixed (ctx, db) migration signature needs to receive the command's writer and colour posture, installed only for the length of a run; a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/mysql/v3 ~ compatible ~ ConnectionConfig ~ added ~ keep ~ the connection details the provider dials, with SafeContext answering them without the password; a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/mysql/v3 ~ compatible ~ NewConnectionConfig ~ added ~ keep ~ builds ConnectionConfig; a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/mysql/v3 ~ compatible ~ (*Provider).OpenContext ~ added ~ keep ~ a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/mysql/v3 ~ compatible ~ (*Provider).OpenForMigration ~ added ~ keep ~ a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/mysql/v3 ~ compatible ~ (*Provider).OpenForMigrationContext ~ added ~ keep ~ a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/mysql/v3 ~ compatible ~ WithInsecure ~ added ~ keep ~ a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/mysql/v3 ~ compatible ~ WithTlsConfig ~ added ~ keep ~ a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/mysql/v3 ~ incompatible ~ (*Provider).Open ~ changed from func(github.com/precision-soft/melody/integrations/bunorm/v3.ConnectionParams, github.com/precision-soft/melody/v3/logging/contract.Logger) (*github.com/uptrace/bun.DB, error) to func(github.com/precision-soft/melody/integrations/bunorm/v3.ConnectionParameters, github.com/precision-soft/melody/v3/logging/contract.Logger) (*github.com/uptrace/bun.DB, error) ~ keep ~ not a compile break: ConnectionParams is a type alias of ConnectionParameters since bunorm v3.5.0, so a released caller compiles unchanged; apidiff reports a type change only because this module's tag resolved an older bunorm where the name was a defined struct
integrations/bunorm/mysql/v3 ~ compatible ~ Unlimited ~ added ~ keep ~ names the bound a zero field no longer lifts, now that zero is read as unset and takes the default: any negative field means no deadline, no connection cap or no recycling; a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/pgsql/v3 ~ compatible ~ ConnectionConfig ~ added ~ keep ~ the connection details the provider dials, with SafeContext answering them without the password; a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/pgsql/v3 ~ compatible ~ NewConnectionConfig ~ added ~ keep ~ builds ConnectionConfig; a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/pgsql/v3 ~ compatible ~ (*Provider).OpenContext ~ added ~ keep ~ a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/pgsql/v3 ~ compatible ~ (*Provider).OpenForMigration ~ added ~ keep ~ a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/pgsql/v3 ~ compatible ~ (*Provider).OpenForMigrationContext ~ added ~ keep ~ a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/pgsql/v3 ~ compatible ~ TimeoutConfig.ReadTimeout ~ added ~ keep ~ the read deadline pgdriver applied invisibly, now a field an operator reads and sets; a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/pgsql/v3 ~ compatible ~ TimeoutConfig.WriteTimeout ~ added ~ keep ~ the write deadline pgdriver applied invisibly, now a field an operator reads and sets; a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/pgsql/v3 ~ compatible ~ RegisterLockerService ~ added ~ keep ~ the plug-and-play registration helper the mysql sibling has carried since the registration pass; this module shipped the advisory-lock Locker at v3.2.0 with no door to publish it, so every consumer named the framework's locker service itself
integrations/bunorm/pgsql/v3 ~ compatible ~ ServiceRegistrar ~ added ~ keep ~ the narrow registrar the helper above takes, declared here rather than imported so the helper can be called with any registrar shape; byte-identical to the mysql sibling's
integrations/bunorm/pgsql/v3 ~ compatible ~ Module ~ added ~ keep ~ the self-registering application module wrapping the helper, the shape the mysql sibling already publishes
integrations/bunorm/pgsql/v3 ~ compatible ~ ModuleConfig ~ added ~ keep ~ the module's configuration: the database to lock on and the AsLocker opt-in, both refused when absent rather than defaulted
integrations/bunorm/pgsql/v3 ~ compatible ~ NewModule ~ added ~ keep ~ the module constructor, the shape the mysql sibling already publishes
integrations/bunorm/pgsql/v3 ~ incompatible ~ (*Provider).Open ~ changed from func(github.com/precision-soft/melody/integrations/bunorm/v3.ConnectionParams, github.com/precision-soft/melody/v3/logging/contract.Logger) (*github.com/uptrace/bun.DB, error) to func(github.com/precision-soft/melody/integrations/bunorm/v3.ConnectionParameters, github.com/precision-soft/melody/v3/logging/contract.Logger) (*github.com/uptrace/bun.DB, error) ~ keep ~ not a compile break: ConnectionParams is a type alias of ConnectionParameters since bunorm v3.5.0, so a released caller compiles unchanged; apidiff reports a type change only because this module's tag resolved an older bunorm where the name was a defined struct
integrations/bunorm/pgsql/v3 ~ compatible ~ Unlimited ~ added ~ keep ~ names the bound a zero field no longer lifts, now that zero is read as unset and takes the default: any negative field means no deadline, no connection cap or no recycling; a compatible addition, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/bunorm/pgsql/v3 ~ compatible ~ NewTimeoutConfigWithDeadlines ~ added ~ keep ~ the compatible twin of step C on v3; v4 carries the reshaped form under the released name
